{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/28253-changelings-in-asia","id":28253,"title":"Changelings in Asia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-11T13:32:39-08:00","id":28253,"title":"Changelings in Asia","content":"So the books don't seem to indicate Asia has Changelings, instead they have Hsien, which are actually little gods, but who the Changelings of the West consider brethren. So one explanation is that the Jade Emperor's Heaven tamed the gods and spirits of dreams into servant spirits. So I guess this means when the Sundering happened they had no Fae who took up the Changeling Way ritual, however we seem to have Asian Denizens of the Dreaming so that seems like it could back this theory. But if a Changeling from say Concordia, or one of the Menehune would travel to Asia wouldn't they still be able to interact with the Dreaming there and form their own Freeholds?<br /> <br /> How do you all handle this? Do you just say there are Changelings in Asia? I've seen people enjoy say Ogre Variants that are say Oni. Or do you have the Hsien and Denizens as the only Fae Equivalents with Foreign Changelings finding a new frontier type of Dreaming?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:46:17-08:00","id":29101,"title":"","content":"The nature of the Asian Dreaming was never really covered, yeah. The Hsien had nothing whatsoever to do with Changeling, and I still have no idea why they were published as a Changeling Book instead of a Werewolf or Mage suppliment or whatever. The books casually mention the viewpoint the Hsien and the Kithain would have towards each other, but there's really no mechanical point where they're likely to interact, except for the one tier 5 Hsien power that lets them go into the Dreaming for no observable thematic reason.<br /> <br /> I just made up a handful of Asian Kiths in my old games, and ignored where they shared design space with existing splats. Like, my Tengu were Changelings, not a branch of the Corax Wereravens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please add signature.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/615-the-hanged-man","name":"The Hanged Man","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"288"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}